 the teacher's call, then the move repeated when asked; day B, DA:Pr4.1.Ka, a look-for: a straight and a curved shape, high and low, big and small, then the group circle formed; DA:Pr4.1.Kb, a look-for: walking speed matched to a slow and a fast drum; DA:Pr4.1.Kc, a look-for: quick, floppy and sharp moves on the called words. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: naming the qualities in words (grade 1), paths and facing (grade 1). Tools: the warm-up card, the elements card in pictures, step cards for each pattern, work cards, Curio Class's own; a beat keeper on the teacher device or the drum. Free path: a pot and a wooden spoon for the drum, chalk or masking tape for spots. Once-a-week path: 10 sessions | First because every later unit needs the safe space, the stop cue and the warm-up, and the elements' words (the dance-warm-up and dance-elements models start here). Longest kindergarten unit: six ids, and every routine of the dance space is learned for the first time | Candidate: the bar's criterion 9 on the set-up and room-back minutes in a classroom with tables pushed back | Hazards and controls: floor cleared and checked for spills and objects before each session; bare feet or soft-soled shoes, never socks on a smooth floor; spots an arm's length apart; no lifts, no jumping from chairs or steps; the freeze cue taught on day 1 and used every session; back-to-back moves with no touching unless both children agree. Connection: physical education K to 2 unit 2 (k-in-place) teaches the in-place moves as motor skill in kindergarten weeks 6 to 10; this unit teaches no motor cue. The Serpentine film is an early film of a white dancer's act; the sensitivity agent checks the Library of Congress item page first. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (moving). |
