ws one other move from the phrase; DA:Re8.1.Ka, a talk item: one move described with an easy dance word. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: a pattern made by repeats (grade 1), moves that stand for an idea (grade 1). Tools: the suggestion card, symbol cards, work cards, the unseen phrase's step card, Curio Class's own. Free path: pencil and scrap paper for symbols. Once-a-week path: 6 sessions | After unit 2 because a change is made to the child's own dance; the dance words come from unit 1. Before unit 4 so the dance shown to families has been changed once and the class has watched as an audience. The try-a-change and look-and-say models start here | Candidate: a third short dance by a living maker from Africa, described and linked, for range in year K | Buchaechum: the sensitivity agent reads a Korean cultural body's page first; no fan dance costume, and children's paper fans carry their own designs. Tap: children do not tap on hard floors in shoes; rhythms are clapped or stamped softly in bare feet. Hazards and controls: as unit 1. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (moving). |
