Each check day is a showing day as in the Scored evidence bullet: six groups of five dance for about four minutes
each while the rest sit as the audience; set-up, warm-up, cool-down and room-back fit the rest of the 40 minutes, and
each child has at most one talk or show item after the group's turn. Every child's evidence is collected once in a
window; no item is scored twice. Days above are band course days (year 1 starts on day 65, year 2 on day 129); the
unit record days named are the unit's last two days before its respond day, as the scope and sequence sets them.

## Cross-subject

The three dance technique rows of K to 2 carry a lean on physical education (data/progressions/arts.csv); no other
row of the band carries a cross_subject lean. STANDARD.md 6 splits the two: physical education teaches the moves as
motor skill, this course teaches dance as an art. The contacts below are named for that split, each with its "if
later" line; all are core courses except physical education, an after-core course named by its own frame (lesson
32: this course assumes no motor cue taught there).

### Physical education, kindergarten to grade 2 (same year, name each other)

The physical education K to 2 frame is written (2026-11-25); its units and weeks are cited from it.

| This course's row and unit | Physical education's row and unit | What each teaches | If later |
|---|---|---|---|
| da-k-technique (unit 1, kindergarten weeks 1 to 10) | k-in-place (unit 2, kindergarten weeks 6 to 10); k-locomotor-basics (unit 1, kindergarten weeks 1 to 6) | Physical education: in-place and traveling moves as motor skill, with cues; dance: copying patterns, safe shared space, the start and stop cue and body parts in relation | Same weeks. The dance unit uses only moves a kindergartner already makes (walk, bend, stretch, twist), shown once as part of a pattern to copy, and teaches no motor cue |
| da-g1-technique, da-g1-elements (unit 5, grade 1 weeks 1 to 9) | g1-dance-moves, g1-dance-ideas (unit 13, grade 1 weeks 23 to 27) | Physical education: dance moves to the beat as motor skill; dance: formations, paths, speeds and quality words | Dance teaches first; physical education unit 13 opens with a retrieval task on them. If a school runs it earlier, the dance unit retrieves its moves and still teaches only the art |
| da-g2-technique, da-g2-elements (unit 9, grade 2 weeks 1 to 9); da-g2-ideas (unit 10, grade 2 weeks 10 to 16) | g2-dance-sequence, g2-show-ideas (unit 21, grade 2 weeks 24 to 26) | Physical education: a linked three-move sequence as motor skill; dance: pathways, symmetry, strong beats and a linked phrase with a central idea | Dance teaches first; physical education unit 21 opens with a retrieval task on them. The dance phrase never asks for physical education's start and end shape cues |

### Mathematics, kindergarten to grade 2 (same year)

| Used here | Contact | If math has not taught it yet |
|---|---|---|
| Units 1, 5 and 9: counting the beat (to 4 in year K and year 1, two- and three-beat counts in year 2) | Counting to 10 and beyond is kindergarten math's first work | The unit counts aloud with the class and claps; no number is written or added |
| Unit 9: symmetrical and uneven shapes | Shapes are named in kindergarten math; symmetry is grade 4 math (4.G.A.3) | The unit says "the same on both sides" and shows it with the body and a folded paper shape; no line of symmetry is drawn or named as math |

No unit asks for measuring, fractions, note values or time signatures (lesson 13).

### English language arts, kindergarten to grade 2 (same year)

Talk about dances and the critique practice collaborative conversation (SL.K.1, SL.1.1, SL.2.1): practiced, not
owned. Unit 8 dances a picture-book story's big ideas, practicing the retelling of key details (RL.1.2), not owned.
If ELA has not yet taught the turn-taking rules, the dance unit's critique card shows them in pictures (look,
listen, one at a time) and the teacher models them on the first critique day.

### Social studies, kindergarten to grade 2

Unit 12's people and place (year 2) sits near social studies grade 2's "Family stories and culture". No lean either
way: the dance units teach the setting they use themselves, on work cards (bar criterion 7), and no child is asked
to explain their own family's culture.

## For the lead

1. **After-core check weeks.** This frame's checks (year K weeks 18 and 26; years 1 and 2 weeks 17 and 25) stay off
   every core check week and follow from the unit days by load. Left for the lead's one calendar pass over all
   after-core frames. `frame.py calendar` (2026-11-25) shows shared weeks: K week 18 (ELD, physical education,
