model_out     : like-me-line; dance-two-ties
words         : personal; present; question; origin; people; place
cross_subject : 
notes         : Make a dance about something personal and explain how the moves show it, answer set questions about a 
                watched dance and move from the answers, and link its movement to the people and place it comes from. 
                What changes: the origin and place of a dance are named, where grade 1 named a familiar experience and 
                another culture. Assessed by a short dance, answers to the set questions with a move made from them, 
                and a spoken tie to its origin, scored on a three-line guide. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial 
                work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, 
                costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it.

