docs/APPROACH-SOURCES.md:88:- Scoring is 0, 1 or 2. Full credit needs all three parts present. One or two of the three earns 1. None earns 0.
docs/APPROACH-SOURCES.md:90:- Criterion 3.1 is worth 10 points in total (9 to 10 meets, 5 to 8 partially meets). Its other indicators: 3a teacher guidance for enacting the materials (2 points), 3b adult-level explanations of the mathematics and how it connects across grades (2 points), 3c year-long scope and sequence with standards correlation, 3d communication to students and caregivers (narrative evidence only), 3f supply list, 3g assessment system and guidance for next steps (2 points), 3h not assessed in mathematics.
docs/APPROACH-SOURCES.md:91:- Related narrative-only indicators later in Gateway 3 (3r to 3u) cover how digital technology is integrated and the teacher guidance for it; relevant because Curio Class is tool-first.
