docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:31:### 1. Kindergarten response work identifies locations of art but omits its uses
docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:34:**LAYER:** standard, propagated into progression and frame  
docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:35:**REPEAT:** yes, semantic drift in an own-words standard is the same kind identified in `arts-words-read-2026-11-20.md`; this particular ID was not corrected there.  
docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:40:The frame asks children to name where art appears. The national kindergarten standard asks them to identify its uses in their surroundings; recognizing nearby art is the preceding pre-kindergarten demand. Naming a mural or pointing to a quilt does not establish what it does for people. [NCAS visual arts standards, PDF page 6](https://www.nationalartsstandards.org/sites/default/files/Visual%20Arts%20at%20a%20Glance%20-%20new%20copyright%20info.pdf).
docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:52:### 2. Several assessment summaries leave owned actions without clear scored evidence
docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:56:**REPEAT:** yes, incomplete links between standards and assessment recur in the earlier arts reviews.  
docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:76:### 3. The claim that the national association gives no weekly minutes is incorrect
docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:79:**LAYER:** standard, propagated into frame  
docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:85:The association’s specific elementary document states at least **50 minutes weekly**. Curio Class provides 80 minutes on the full path and 40 on the short path. The short path therefore falls 10 minutes below that published minimum. [Elementary visual arts opportunity-to-learn standards, PDF pages 3 and 4](https://www.arteducators.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/OTL-Elementary_Visual_Media_Arts_Program.pdf).
docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:87:**Why it matters:** The current statement hides the short path’s time gap from schools and contradicts Cory’s decision to publish source-checked time figures.
docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:91:> The national visual arts educators’ association recommends at least 50 minutes weekly for elementary visual arts. This course provides 80 minutes weekly on the full path and 40 on the short path, respectively 30 minutes above and 10 minutes below that figure.
docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:93:Correct the elementary visual arts entry and concluding sentence in `STANDARD.md` section 3.4. Do not extend this elementary finding to media arts or middle school without checking their specific documents. Keep the settled 64-session and 32-session paths.
