docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:135:## Coverage, days and seams
docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:143:The full-path allocations are reasonable: 18/16/14/12 sessions in K and grade 1, and 16/16/16/12 in grade 2. Studio routines justify the longer opening units; the final units use retained work. No unit is demonstrably far over or under its load at frame level.
docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:145:The short-path unit counts total 28 sessions per year, leaving four for course checks and response. They preserve the stated check weeks, although the following respond session occurs a week later than on the full path.
docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:149:## Arts lens checklist at frame level
docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:161:| Assessment includes kept work, growth and self-assessment | Met in the design; full coverage needs finding 2 |
docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:168:## What is right and should be preserved
docs/reviews/frame-visual-arts-grades-k-to-2-codex-2026-11-25.md:170:Preserve the three complete years, the four-unit progression within each year, the concrete technique steps, the distinction between artistic responding and respond days, and the critique followed by revision. Keep the paper and home paths, locally held portfolios, invented alternatives to private-life disclosures, and explicit notice that leaving out a unit removes its standards claim.
