- **Logic model (one page in the scope and sequence).** Inputs: two 40-minute sessions a week, a cleared floor, step
  cards, work cards, a drum or the voice. Activities: moves, elements and tools taught in steps, dances watched with
  their setting, research and sources turned into movement, making and rehearsing with a critique and a change, a
  showing each unit. Outputs: a portfolio folder of 12 pieces over the band with reflections, 12 showings, two marks
  a unit per student on the main look-for. Outcome claimed: met marks on the year's 21 ids and growth on the
  look-fors. Nothing here has been tried with children, and Curio Class makes no claim that arts study raises any
  other result (APPROACH "Sources").

## Seams

### Picked up from Dance, grades K to 2

Each grade 3 row assumes its thread's grade 2 row, last used one grade back in the grade 2 year of Dance, grades K to
2 (band days 129 to 192), so it opens as a retrieval task inside day 2 of its unit, carrying its ten-minute reteach
for a student or class that did not take that year (by course order, lesson 32).

| Thread | Grade 2 row (Dance K to 2 unit, band days) | Grade 3 row that picks it up (unit here) | What grade 3 does with it |
|---|---|---|---|
| Body and safe space | da-g2-technique (unit 9, days 129 to 146) | da-g3-technique (unit 1) | Pathways and adjusting become a copied sequence with the body aligned, partner level and path changes, and recall coached in pairs with a self-check |
| Dance elements | da-g2-elements (unit 9, days 129 to 146) | da-g3-elements (unit 1) | Direction, symmetry and strong beats become distance, three dimensions, filled and empty space, and an improvisation that fills a set count |
| Ideas | da-g2-ideas (unit 10, days 147 to 160) | da-g3-ideas (unit 2) | Gathered sources become a starting point of the student's own, and a movement challenge solved |
| Connecting | da-g2-connect (unit 12, days 179 to 192) | da-g3-connect (unit 2) | A dance's people and place become a first research question about a dance's view on an issue, and moves linked to their culture |
| Shape of a dance | da-g2-form (unit 10, days 147 to 160) | da-g3-form (unit 3) | A central idea in the middle becomes choreographic tools (repetition, reversal, accumulation) and AB and ABA forms |
| Watching dances | da-g2-respond (unit 11, days 163 to 176) | da-g3-respond (unit 3) | Clues across styles become two traditions compared side by side, and clues tied to a main idea |
| Changing and recording | da-g2-revise (unit 11, days 163 to 176) | da-g3-revise (unit 4) | A chosen change and level symbols become a change made after partner feedback, and a floor map of paths |
| Performing space | da-g2-stage (unit 12, days 179 to 192) | da-g3-stage (unit 4) | Separate zones and a staging extra become named stage areas and a first costume, music, scenery or light choice |

Each pick-up above is answered at both ends in data/progressions/arts.csv (the grade 3 rows' `assumes` cells).

### Inside the band: year to year

Each row of years 4 and 5 assumes the year before's row in its thread (one grade back), so it opens as a retrieval
task inside day 2 of its unit.

| Thread | Year 3 row (unit, band days) | Year 4 row that picks it up (unit) | Year 5 row that picks it up (unit) | What changes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Body and safe space | da-g3-technique (unit 1, days 1 to 16) | da-g4-technique (unit 5): balance, a strengthening routine, moving together on a cue | da-g5-technique (unit 9) retrieves da-g4-technique (unit 5, days 65 to 80): a run of phrases, safe habits, ensemble goals | Alignment and partner safety, then balance and cues, then an ensemble rehearsing to goals |
| Dance elements | da-g3-elements (unit 1, days 1 to 16) | da-g4-elements (unit 5): eye contact, a drum part, uneven rhythms, energy in words | da-g5-elements (unit 9) retrieves da-g4-elements (unit 5, days 65 to 80): ground and air paths, body percussion, tight against flowing | Space, time and energy judged, then answered in rhythm and described, then contrasted and projected |
| Ideas | da-g3-ideas (unit 2, days 17 to 32) | da-g4-ideas (unit 6): an idea card, a challenge invented for a partner | da-g5-ideas (unit 10) retrieves da-g4-ideas (unit 6, days 81 to 96): several sources, several challenges in a group | Solving a set challenge, then inventing one, then building a body of material |
| Connecting | da-g3-connect (unit 2, days 17 to 32) | da-g4-connect (unit 6): a school topic from several sources, a style and its era | da-g5-connect (unit 10) retrieves da-g4-connect (unit 6, days 81 to 96): another subject's topic compared, opposing themes, a period's ideas | One research question, then a topic from sources, then learning in two subjects compared |
| Shape of a dance | da-g3-form (unit 3, days 35 to 50) | da-g4-form (unit 7): a tool altered, a study around one main idea | da-g5-form (unit 11) retrieves da-g4-form (unit 7, days 99 to 114): several tools altered together, a study that speaks without words | Named forms, then a study with a main idea, then a study whose tools sharpen it together |
| Watching dances | da-g3-respond (unit 3, days 35 to 50) | da-g4-respond (unit 7): patterns across dances, styles in one genre, setting as a clue, what is artistic | da-g5-respond (unit 11) retrieves da-g4-respond (unit 7, days 99 to 114): meaning from patterns, a chosen style compared, traits tied to elements | Two traditions compared, then styles inside a genre, then meaning and traits defined |
| Changing and recording | da-g3-revise (unit 4, days 53 to 64) | da-g4-revise (unit 8): comments and reflection, a relationship sketch | da-g5-revise (unit 12) retrieves da-g4-revise (unit 8, days 117 to 128): peer suggestions, a change log | Feedback drives a change, then reflection joins it, then the changes are logged |
| Performing space | da-g3-stage (unit 4, days 53 to 64) | da-g4-stage (unit 8): a gym or lawn planned as a stage, production elements | da-g5-stage (unit 12) retrieves da-g4-stage (unit 8, days 117 to 128): one dance adapted to two venues | Stage areas named, then a plain space planned as a stage, then one dance fitted to two spaces |

